    <briefdescription>
<para>Memory allocation and management errors. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="classcslt_1_1MemoryError" kindref="compound">MemoryError</ref> represents errors related to memory allocation failures, reallocation issues, out-of-memory conditions, and alignment problems.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Example Usage:</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Using<sp/>default<sp/>message</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">throw</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="classcslt_1_1MemoryError_1a8103a9a2e63627c1a0bdbf98ddd4a8e8" kindref="member">MemoryError</ref>();<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>&quot;Memory<sp/>allocation<sp/>failed&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Using<sp/>custom<sp/>message</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keywordflow">throw</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/><ref refid="classcslt_1_1MemoryError_1a8103a9a2e63627c1a0bdbf98ddd4a8e8" kindref="member">MemoryError</ref>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;Failed<sp/>to<sp/>allocate<sp/>1024<sp/>bytes&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
